// Ch1 C1-15 "Cutscene: Going under". O18: Hullgnaw's last coil slides off the broken net-pen, the
// children are on the bridge to the keel-hull; Rhen looks up and the wall is here, filling the frame,
// the sky still blue above it. Across the water on the keel-hull, Kell's beacon lamp is STILL LIT.
// The water comes over the frame before it goes out: he never sees her go under, and neither does
// the player. U10: under, the storm's underwater look (no god rays, churned dark), and all round him
// lamps going out above and their light coming down: held motes sinking past him, dozens, then
// hundreds. His lantern still burns on his shoulder (oil_lamp, the only warm light). U11: looking
// down into the dark, a man's voice singing the whole current-song from C1-06, far below. He stops
// fighting the water and listens. That's all. Then black, the VO, silence, and a 3 s hold; the
// chapter flow then goes to ch02/haluna Beach, where Cutscene A fades in on its first line.
// Watches (ADR 0017, ADR 0022, act3_ending §0 rule 8): no figure guides him into or out of the
// storm, and nothing carries him through time or space; the song is heard, never seen, sings no
// words of Lamptongue and none to Rhen; the current-song is NOT the Hush lullaby; the motes sink.
// Nothing lifts in Ch1. U11 shows no one.
title: ch01_going_under
location: ch01/oruvel
---
@letterbox on
@camera O18
@sfx undertow_wall_roar
@wait 2.0
Rhen [afraid]: Go! Don't look back, go! #line:ch01_under_001
@sfx beacon_lamp_gutter
@wait 1.5
@fade out 0.4
@camera U10
// M3-CIN-1232 (PC GPU QA, the dive's gaps): U10 and U11 are under the water now (Oruvel's UnderwaterRig), not on
// the waterline; the warm light is his lantern (the stage's dive_lamp, below the lens), and the motes sink through
// the frame from under_rhen rather than at the player, who is still up on the pen. U11 looks down at a slant, so
// the last of the light is at the top of the frame, and more of it sinks past into the dark (under_deep).
@light DiveLamp on
// PC pass 7 row 75: U10/U11 were near-black. A cool key under the hull's belly and a rim on its near edge give the
// hull a readable shape; both go out with the lantern.
@light HullRim on
@light HullKey on
@music going_under fade=0.5
@fade in 1.5
@vfx glimmer_held at=under_rhen count=60 drift=down_seaward
@wait 4.0
@vfx glimmer_held at=under_deep count=30 drift=down_seaward
@camera U11
@wait 17.4
@fade out 2.5
@light DiveLamp off 2.5
@light HullRim off 2.5
@light HullKey off 2.5
@music silence fade=2.0
Narrator(rhen) [neutral]: My father used to sing the currents. I hadn't heard it in eleven years. Then nothing. #line:ch01_under_002 #vo
@wait 3.0
===
